1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,824
Trading bots ask for a lot of trust.

2
00:00:02,854 --> 00:00:05,285
Most want your keys, or a balance they can

3
00:00:05,315 --> 00:00:06,748
move however they like.

4
00:00:06,778 --> 00:00:09,404
And when one goes wrong, there's no brake.

5
00:00:09,434 --> 00:00:12,411
XORR is a council of AI agents that trades for

6
00:00:12,441 --> 00:00:14,849
you, inside a limit you sign and the chain

7
00:00:14,879 --> 00:00:16,263
enforces.

8
00:00:16,293 --> 00:00:18,756
One hold stops every agent, on chain.

9
00:00:18,786 --> 00:00:21,844
And it's built on Monad, because a council

10
00:00:21,874 --> 00:00:23,946
that votes, trades and settles in about a

11
00:00:23,976 --> 00:00:26,105
second needs a chain that's final in half of

12
00:00:26,135 --> 00:00:26,981
one.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,027
This is the live app on Monad testnet, in a

14
00:00:38,057 --> 00:00:40,883
browser. A passkey makes the account, and

15
00:00:40,913 --> 00:00:43,012
nothing that can sign is stored.

16
00:00:44,312 --> 00:00:47,010
Built on Monad shows what XORR reads from the

17
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,402
chain itself, live.

18
00:00:49,432 --> 00:00:50,366
Every new block:

19
00:00:50,396 --> 00:00:52,766
proposed, voted, final.

20
00:00:52,796 --> 00:00:54,984
Voted in about three hundred milliseconds, and

21
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:57,024
final in about half a second.

22
00:00:57,054 --> 00:01:00,774
Monad's txpool, the P256 precompile that

23
00:01:00,804 --> 00:01:03,224
checks your passkey, native staking.

24
00:01:03,254 --> 00:01:05,105
Each one read now, and each saying where it

25
00:01:05,135 --> 00:01:06,038
runs.

26
00:01:07,338 --> 00:01:09,409
Here's a real round from tonight.

27
00:01:09,439 --> 00:01:11,882
A wallet we seeded ourselves, and labelled as

28
00:01:11,912 --> 00:01:14,460
team-seeded, put fifty dollars of bitcoin to

29
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:15,746
the council.

30
00:01:15,776 --> 00:01:18,056
The Price desk checks Chainlink on Monad

31
00:01:18,086 --> 00:01:19,717
against Perpl's order book.

32
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:21,446
Risk reads the owner's limits.

33
00:01:21,476 --> 00:01:23,673
Trend and Perps read the market.

34
00:01:23,703 --> 00:01:26,232
And Kimi weighs the desks, and says why.

35
00:01:27,532 --> 00:01:29,685
Approved, four to nothing.

36
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:31,519
The order went to Perpl through the owner's

37
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:34,259
own desk: an account the agent can trade, but

38
00:01:34,289 --> 00:01:35,893
never withdraw from.

39
00:01:35,923 --> 00:01:38,545
Here's that fill, on Monad testnet.

40
00:01:39,845 --> 00:01:42,717
The agents only run strategies that survived.

41
00:01:42,747 --> 00:01:45,295
Three hundred and thirteen were backtested.

42
00:01:45,325 --> 00:01:47,652
Ten got through four tests on data they never

43
00:01:47,682 --> 00:01:48,643
saw.

44
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:52,108
And when you've had enough, one hold removes

45
00:01:52,138 --> 00:01:55,318
XORR's key from your desk, on chain.

46
00:01:55,714 --> 00:01:57,751
After that, no agent can trade, whatever any

47
00:01:57,781 --> 00:01:59,234
server says.

48
00:01:59,264 --> 00:02:01,092
This is that removal, from our testnet proof

49
00:02:01,122 --> 00:02:01,932
run.

50
00:02:03,232 --> 00:02:06,789
XORR. A council of AI agents trades for you on

51
00:02:06,819 --> 00:02:09,037
Monad, and one hold stops it on chain.

